WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:07.319
Iran has conducted combat operations

00:00:07.319 --> 00:00:09.300
beyond its borders with conventional, as

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:11.370
well as advisory forces, in Iraq and

00:00:11.370 --> 00:00:13.349
Syria since 2015. We've observed this

00:00:13.349 --> 00:00:14.969
development by tracking Iranian troop

00:00:14.969 --> 00:00:17.220
rotations in Farsi and Arabic media, and

00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:19.109
on social media. Iran used to rely on

00:00:19.109 --> 00:00:20.910
proxies is guided by the clandestine Quds

00:00:20.910 --> 00:00:23.039
Force. It hasn't sent the conventional

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:24.420
Islamic Revolutionary Guards Corps

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:26.550
beyond its borders since the nineteen

00:00:26.550 --> 00:00:28.470
eighties. Its regular military, the Artesh,

00:00:28.470 --> 00:00:30.359
has never fought abroad.

00:00:30.359 --> 00:00:32.669
That's changed. Parts of IRGC brigades

00:00:32.669 --> 00:00:34.500
have fought in Syria alongside Hezbollah

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:37.079
and Iraqi militias. Artesh units are

00:00:37.079 --> 00:00:39.270
fighting in Syria. Even the internal-

00:00:39.270 --> 00:00:40.620
security-come-morality-police-

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:43.200
organization, called the Basij, has sent

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:45.360
combat units to Syria. Iran is creating

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:47.039
the ability to lead and fight with a

00:00:47.039 --> 00:00:48.629
coalition of tens of thousands of

00:00:48.629 --> 00:00:50.610
proxy forces, hundreds of miles from

00:00:50.610 --> 00:00:52.260
its borders, for the first time in its

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:54.329
history, and its asking Russia to sell it

00:00:54.329 --> 00:00:56.670
advanced aircraft, tanks, and anti-shipping

00:00:56.670 --> 00:00:58.680
missiles that would give it one of the

00:00:58.680 --> 00:01:01.079
region's most powerful militaries. The US must

00:01:01.079 --> 00:01:04.229
take determined – but not hasty – action to

00:01:04.229 --> 00:01:06.669
address this new challenge from an old adversary.

00:01:08.120 --> 00:01:09.260
If you liked this video, check

00:01:09.270 --> 00:01:11.100
out CriticalThreats.org for more

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:12.600
coverage on the challenges facing the

00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:14.520
United States abroad. We track threats

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:17.100
from al-Qaeda to Iran. Also, let us know

00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:19.049
what other topics you'd like AEI scholars

00:01:19.049 --> 00:01:23.530
to cover in 60 seconds.

